   approach="Keep a second, *shadow* stack whose top is always the minimum of everything currently in the main stack. On every push, push `min(newValue, mins.top())`. On every pop, pop both.\n\nPush onto `mins` **unconditionally**, even when the new value is not a new minimum. That keeps the two stacks exactly the same height, so `pop()` is a single line and the two can never desynchronise.",
