   approach="This direction cannot be made amortised O(1) — one of the two operations has to be O(n), and you choose which. The tidiest is a **single queue with a rotation on push**: push the new element, then move every *previous* element from the front to the back, so the newest element ends up at the front where `pop` can reach it.\n\nOne container, O(n) push, O(1) pop.",
