   problem="Implement a fixed-capacity FIFO queue on an array, reusing the space freed by dequeues. All operations O(1).",
   approach="Store `front` and `count` and **derive** the rear as `(front + count) % cap`. Enqueue writes at that derived slot and increments `count`; dequeue just walks `front = (front + 1) % cap` forward and decrements.\n\nThe modulus is what turns the array into a ring, so the free space behind `front` is reused instead of being lost.",
