   approach="Run the standard next-greater pass over `nums2`, recording the answers in a hash map from value to next-greater-value. Then look each element of `nums1` up.\n\nThe stack holds values in **decreasing** order — those are the elements still waiting for something bigger. When a bigger value arrives, everything smaller on the stack has found its answer, so pop them all and record.",
